      "source": [
        "### 3. Implement Iterative Deepening Depth-Limited Search (IDDLS)\n",
        "\n",
        "IDDLS works by repeatedly performing Depth-Limited Search (DLS) with increasing depth limits until the goal is found. This combines the completeness of BFS with the space efficiency of DFS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "02b5fe71"
      },
      "source": [
        "def dls(current_state, goal_state, limit, visited_states):\n",
        "    if current_state == goal_state:\n",
        "        return current_state\n",
        "\n",
        "    if current_state.depth == limit:\n",
        "        return None  # Reached depth limit\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Add current state to visited for this DLS iteration to prevent cycles within the limit\n",
        "    visited_states.add(current_state)\n",
        "\n",
        "    for move_pos in current_state.get_possible_moves():\n",
        "        new_state = current_state.apply_move(move_pos)\n",
        "        if new_state not in visited_states: # Only explore if not visited in this path\n",
        "            result = dls(new_state, goal_state, limit, visited_states)\n",
        "            if result:\n",
        "                return result\n",
        "    return None\n",
        "\n",
        "def iddls(initial_state, goal_state, max_depth=20): # Increased max_depth for more complex puzzles\n",
        "    for limit in range(max_depth + 1):\n",
        "        print(f\"Trying depth limit: {limit}\")\n",
        "        visited_states = set() # Reset visited states for each depth limit\n",
        "        result = dls(initial_state, goal_state, limit, visited_states)\n",
        "        if result:\n",
        "            return result\n",
        "    return None # No solution found within max_depth\n"
      ],
      "execution_count": 4,
      "outputs": []
    },
